# autonomy-grade — the auto/human disposition decided by the agent's granted grade
# (specification v0.6). `deploy` is a source gate requiring autonomy grade L3 to act
# unattended. An agent granted L3 releases automatically; an agent granted only L1
# (or ungraded) is withheld for human oversight (cf. AI Act Art. 14). The grade is a
# config attribute of the agent and the checkpoint — not a token field, not guardable.
#
# The ladder (L0..L4) and what each level means are policy (vocabulary/grades.json,
# remappable); the language owns only the order and this gating rule.
actor agent grade L3
gate  deploy risk high grade L3 grant agent
cord  agent  -> deploy
cord  deploy -> master